Architecture: SDD

Purpose:
  Define the internal architecture of the .sdd system itself — which
  components exist inside .sdd/, how they relate, and which relationships
  are allowed. This is NOT the project's technical architecture (stack,
  module isolation, layers) — that lives in project/architecture.sdd
  (bax Note aşağıda, adı bənzər olsa da miqyası fərqlidir).

Owns:
  .sdd/

Components:

  PROJECT:
    path: ../PROJECT.sdd
    role: Root entry point / router (bax PROJECT.sdd -> Rules R1-R3)

  PROJECT_MODEL:
    path: ../project
    role: Project knowledge model (WHAT/WHY/WHERE)

  ARCHITECTURE:
    path: ../architecture
    role: SDD system architecture definitions (this file)

  CHAINS:
    path: ../chains
    role: Execution chains (feature-per-chain, STEP 8)

  SKILLS:
    path: ../skills
    role: Engineering skills (HOW, STEP 9)

  PROMPTS:
    path: ../prompts
    role: Prompt intelligence (inbox, analysis)

  TASKS:
    path: ../tasks
    role: Work management (active/planned/completed)

  DECISIONS:
    path: ../decisions
    role: Human decisions

  STATE:
    path: ../state
    role: System state


Relationships:

  PROJECT
    -> PROJECT_MODEL

  PROJECT
    -> ARCHITECTURE

  PROJECT_MODEL
    -> CHAINS

  CHAINS
    -> SKILLS

  PROMPTS
    -> TASKS

  TASKS
    -> STATE

  DECISIONS
    -> ARCHITECTURE
    -> PROJECT_MODEL
    -> CHAINS


Allowed:

  PROJECT:
    may_reference:
      PROJECT_MODEL
      ARCHITECTURE
      CHAINS
      SKILLS
      PROMPTS
      TASKS
      DECISIONS
      STATE

  PROJECT_MODEL:
    may_reference:
      ARCHITECTURE
      CHAINS
      SKILLS
      TASKS
      DECISIONS

  CHAINS:
    may_reference:
      SKILLS
      TASKS
      STATE
      DECISIONS

  TASKS:
    may_reference:
      PROJECT_MODEL
      CHAINS
      SKILLS
      DECISIONS
      STATE

  PROMPTS:
    may_reference:
      PROJECT_MODEL
      ARCHITECTURE
      CHAINS
      SKILLS
      TASKS
      DECISIONS


Forbidden:

  SKILLS:
    MUST NOT redefine PROJECT architecture.

  TASKS:
    MUST NOT redefine global SDD architecture.

  PROMPTS:
    MUST NOT silently modify architecture or global rules.

  STATE:
    MUST NOT define architecture.

  PROJECT_MODEL:
    MUST NOT contain engineering skill instructions.

  ARCHITECTURE:
    MUST NOT contain implementation code.


Principles:

  SeparationOfConcerns:
    Each SDD component MUST own one responsibility.

  SingleSourceOfTruth:
    A fact MUST have one authoritative SDD owner.

  ExplicitReference:
    Cross-component knowledge MUST use references.

  Locality:
    Detailed knowledge MUST live as close as possible to
    the component that owns it.

  NoDuplication:
    The same knowledge MUST NOT be copied across multiple SDD files.

  Traceability:
    Every task MUST be traceable to a project element,
    chain stage or decision.

  HumanControl:
    Global architecture changes require human approval — this is the
    same rule as PROJECT.sdd -> Rules [R9]/[R11], not a separate
    definition; this file does not restate it as new authority, it just
    applies it to the SDD component graph above.

State: +
  (STEP 3 tamamlandı — bax PROJECT.sdd -> Rules [R10]: mərhələ bitəndə
  state işarələnməlidir.)

Note:
  (prompt/new/20.md) Bu fayl `.sdd`-in ÖZ komponentlərinin (PROJECT,
  PROJECT_MODEL, ARCHITECTURE, CHAINS, SKILLS, PROMPTS, TASKS, DECISIONS,
  STATE) bir-biri ilə necə əlaqələndiyini təsvir edir — "meta" səviyyədədir.

  Fərqləndirmə (adı toqquşduğu üçün vacib): `project/architecture.sdd`
  layihənin öz texniki arxitekturasıdır (stack, ModuleIsolation,
  LayerArchitecture — FE/BE/DB necə çağırır) və bu fayldan TAMAMILƏ
  ayrıdır. Bu fayl heç vaxt `project/architecture.sdd`-in məzmununu
  təkrarlamır (bax NoDuplication prinsipi yuxarıda) — sadəcə
  PROJECT_MODEL komponenti kimi ona referans verir.

  `project/architecture.sdd` özü hələ köhnə `protocol/symbols.sdd`,
  `protocol/rules.sdd` ifadələrinə istinad edir (bax .sdd/PROJECT.sdd ->
  Note, "məlum, hələ təmizlənməmiş qalıq") — bu fayl həmin problemi HƏLL
  ETMİR, çünki fərqli bir sənəddir və next-gated qaydaya görə yalnız
  uyğun bir "next" gələndə düzələcək.

  Mənbə (prompt/new/20.md) template-i demək olar ki, olduğu kimi
  saxlanıldı, çünki Components/Relationships/Allowed/Forbidden/Principles
  strukturu artıq özü aydın və tam idi; əlavə edilən yeganə best-practice
  hissələr bu Note və `HumanControl`-un R9/R11-ə açıq istinadı, həmçinin
  `State:` sətridir (R10-a uyğun).
